PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B1,A3} 

The black stones form three disconnected groups: {A2}, {B3,B4}, and {C1,C2}. The last of these has exactly two liberties (B1 and B2). White's move at B1 places that group in atari. Black has no legal reply that adds a liberty or connects out (B2 is suicide because the adjacent white stone at B1 still possesses the external liberty A1). White therefore answers at B2 on the next turn and captures the two stones regardless of Black's intervening play elsewhere.

The remaining black stones {A2,B3,B4} likewise have a shared vital point at A3. White's move there reduces their collective liberties to one and initiates a forcing sequence that captures them irrespective of Black's replies. No other first move by White leads to an unconditional capture of any black group.

