11.text:
{B1} 

The only forcing first move is B1, which ataris the two-liberty group {C1,C2} (remaining liberty B2). B2 is suicide for Black (fills no White liberty and leaves the stone with zero liberties), so Black has no saving reply. White therefore captures at B2 on the next turn irrespective of Black's play elsewhere.  

B2 fails as a forcing move: after White B2 the same group is left with one liberty at B1, but Black can legally occupy B1 and capture the invading stone. All other candidate points (A3, etc.) leave at least one Black group with two or more liberties or permit an immediate connection/escape, so they do not initiate an unconditional capture sequence.

