4.text:
The positions show C1+C2 as an isolated 2-liberty Black group (exactly B1/B2). White B1 fills one liberty and appears to leave B2 as suicide, but that evaluation is incomplete: B2 simultaneously joins C1-C2 into the A2-B3-B4 chain (via the newly occupied B2), and the resulting single component gains the external liberty at A1. The move is therefore legal. The combined shape then possesses multiple liberties plus eye space that White cannot reduce in one move, so the stones live under optimal Black replies.

B2 as a first move is immediate self-atari for White. Every other empty intersection either leaves C1-C2 with two liberties, permits an instant safe connection/capture of the invader, or fails to reduce any Black group to a single liberty. Consequently no forcing first move exists.

